e of *this repository's* generated artifacts."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":69847,"cache_read_input_tokens":835,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":69847},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e49b2b87-17d7-4d8a-a105-c125abd095e2","uuid":"a819ff39-b850-440a-ac3b-8da947f73296","request_id":"req_011CenrZAat3Zzpxu8HXHiiU"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CenrZCEbkZBqKWkbndBfd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014RnKx217Z4xSJnfe9oFbaS","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"verdict":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","findings":["MAJOR — Stale-generated-output loophole: the narrow command set omits two declared freshness enforcers for artifacts derived from paths the selector marks narrowable. Seam: `scripts/check_changed.py` `commands()` (the four post-pytest commands: `derive_stage --check`, `trace --strict --no-placeholders --strict-schema`, `gen_trajectory --check`, `gen_trajectory --status --check`) together with `REGISTRY_DATA`/`GENERATED` membership. Scenario A (self-demonstrating on this very slice): the only edit is `module` values in `docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml` (`traj_render.py` -> `rendering/traj_render.py`). That path is in `REGISTRY_DATA`, the shape is str->str, so `data_only` is True and `select` returns `core+boundary`. The P9R execution record states this exact edit required regenerating the derived component inventory (\"`gen_components.py --root . --check` passes after regenerating the derived component list\"), yet no narrow command runs `gen_components.py --check`, so a committed-stale `docs/requirements/components.derived.toml` yields a green local bar. Scenario B: edit a `OneLine`/`Recommendation` value in `docs/requirements/open-items.toml` (also in `REGISTRY_DATA`, shape unchanged) -> `core+boundary`; `docs/open-items.html` — a committed generated owner surface with its own `open-items` harness step, named as such in `traj_status.status_block` — is never regenerated or checked. `--status --check` only byte-compares the status block, not that second rendered surface. This is precisely the contract's \"Keep required generated-output freshness when source data changes\" and \"Classify other generated HTML, including open-items views, deliberately rather than leaving an unnoticed second rendering path\". Inverted incentive that makes it worse: neither `docs/open-items.html` nor `docs/requirements/components.derived.toml` is in `GENERATED`, so an author who *does* regenerate them lands an unclassified path -> Full, while leaving them stale is the only route to a narrow result. Smallest root-cause repair: add those two paths to `GENERATED` (companion-only, so they still cannot authorize narrowing alone, exactly like `PROJECT_STATE.html`) and append their existing `--check` invocations to the narrow list in `commands()`. No new mechanism, no impact engine — two list entries and two commands.","SUB-POINT of the above (same repair site, MINOR): `REGISTRY_DATA` lists `docs/requirements/components.toml`, which matches no path in this repository — the component carrier here is `components.derived.toml`. As written the entry is dead membership; and the derived carrier must not simply be moved into `REGISTRY_DATA` (that would let a hand-edit of a generated file narrow). Classify it as a generated companion per the repair above, and drop or correct the dead `components.toml` entry so the whitelist states what it actually covers."],"basis":"Read the LLR-AND-RENDERING section 2 contract, the P9R work package, the complete execution record, the full `check_changed.py` source and its 31-case test module, `traj_display.py`, `traj_status.py`, the facade header/import gate/re-exports/`build_html`/`main`, the `process_panel` seam, the critique render-surface source, and the tracked product/test diffs. Verified each of the five previously-repaired defects independently rather than restating them: the `process_panel` default fourth argument is safe because `load_stage_record` returns `{}` not `None`; `_stage_facts` is stage-only and its test is non-vacuous (a deliberately malformed SR registry does not break it); `status_block`/`build_html` each take exactly one snapshot, so there is no duplicate or contradictory read; the render surface covers facade + root `traj_*